# polyglots: glossary term not used: "email" -> "correo electrónico"
# polyglots: The glossary term 'email' must be translated as 'correo electrónico'.
#. Short description.
#, gp-priority: high
msgid ""
"Send WordPress email through a locked MailBridgeAPI mailbox without storing "
"SMTP credentials, with delivery logs, diagnostics and remote visibility."
msgstr ""
"Envía correos electrónicos de WordPress mediante un buzón bloqueado de "
"MailBridgeAPI sin almacenar credenciales SMTP, con registros de entrega, "
"diagnósticos y supervisión remota."

# polyglots: glossary term not used: "email" -> "correo electrónico"; "review" -> "reseña / valoración"
# polyglots: The glossary term 'email' must be translated as 'correo electrónico'.
#. Screenshot description.
msgid ""
"Review sent email, delivery failures and mailbox health from the "
"MailBridgeAPI mobile app on Android and iOS."
msgstr ""
"Consulta los correos electrónicos enviados, los fallos de entrega y el "
"estado del buzón desde la aplicación móvil MailBridgeAPI para Android e iOS."

# polyglots: glossary term not used: "email" -> "correo electrónico"
# polyglots: The glossary term 'email' must be translated as 'correo electrónico'.
#. Screenshot description.
msgid ""
"Monitor connected mailboxes, email activity, sending source and operational "
"health from the MailBridgeAPI web dashboard."
msgstr ""
"Supervisa los buzones conectados, la actividad del correo electrónico, el "
"origen de los envíos y el estado operativo desde el escritorio web de "
"MailBridgeAPI."

# polyglots: glossary term not used: "authentication" -> "identificación"
# polyglots: "autentica" -> "identificar / identificación" (Glossary: authenticate/authentication - use "identificar/identificación", never "autenticar/autenticación".)
# polyglots: The glossary term 'authentication' must be translated as 'identificación'.
#. Found in faq paragraph.
msgid ""
"No. It is used once for the secure authentication request and then "
"discarded. The resulting session token and API keys are encrypted before "
"database storage."
msgstr ""
"No. Se utiliza una sola vez para la solicitud de identificación segura y "
"después se descarta. El token de sesión y las claves API resultantes se "
"cifran antes de guardarlos en la base de datos."

# polyglots: glossary term not used: "authenticate" -> "identificar"; "only" -> "solo" / "solo / solamente"
# polyglots: "autentica" -> "identificar / identificación" (Glossary: authenticate/authentication - use "identificar/identificación", never "autenticar/autenticación".)
# polyglots: The glossary term 'authenticate' must be translated as 'identificar'.
# polyglots: the model's fix was kept, but brought in what the submitted text did not have: custom ("identificarse" -> "acceder" (Glossary: login - "Identificarse" is incorrect; use "Acceder".))
#. Found in faq paragraph.
msgid ""
"No. Once a mailbox is selected, the plugin stores only that selected "
"mailbox and no longer displays the account mailbox list. An administrator "
"must disconnect and authenticate again to choose another mailbox."
msgstr ""
"No. Cuando se selecciona un buzón, el plugin guarda únicamente ese buzón y "
"deja de mostrar la lista de buzones de la cuenta. Un administrador debe "
"desconectarse e identificarse de nuevo para elegir otro buzón."

# polyglots: The translation is missing the closing quotation mark for the question.
# polyglots: the proposed fix was unchanged from what was submitted
#. Found in faq header.
#, fuzzy
msgid "Why is a message shown as an error?"
msgstr "¿Por qué se muestra un mensaje como error?"

# polyglots: glossary term not used: "supported" -> "compatible"
# polyglots: The glossary specifies 'compatible' for 'supported'.
#. Found in faq header.
msgid "Which attachments are supported?"
msgstr "¿Qué archivos adjuntos son compatibles?"

# polyglots: glossary term not used: "email" -> "correo electrónico"
# polyglots: The glossary specifies 'correo electrónico' for 'email'.
#. Found in faq header.
msgid "Does the plugin store email content?"
msgstr "¿Almacena el plugin el contenido del correo electrónico?"

# polyglots: glossary term not used: "email" -> "correo electrónico"
# polyglots: The glossary specifies 'correo electrónico' for 'email'.
#. Found in installation list item.
msgid ""
"Trigger a normal WordPress or WooCommerce email, then verify it under "
"<strong>MailBridgeAPI &gt; Sent emails</strong>."
msgstr ""
"Provoca el envío de un correo electrónico normal de WordPress o WooCommerce "
"y compruébalo después en <strong>MailBridgeAPI &gt; Correos "
"enviados</strong>."

# polyglots: glossary term not used: "email" -> "correo electrónico"
# polyglots: Glossary: email address - use "dirección de correo electrónico".
# polyglots: The glossary specifies 'dirección de correo electrónico' for 'email address'.
#. Found in installation list item.
msgid "Enter the email address and password used for your MailBridgeAPI dashboard."
msgstr ""
"Introduce la dirección de correo electrónico y la contraseña que utilizas "
"para el escritorio de MailBridgeAPI."

# polyglots: glossary term not used: "bcc" -> "cco"; "code" -> "código" / "programar"
# polyglots: Glossary: BCC - use the Spanish abbreviation "CCO" (Con Copia Oculta). Ignore header names in code.
# polyglots: The glossary requires 'BCC' to be translated as 'CCO'.
#. Found in description paragraph.
msgid ""
"The plugin intercepts <code>wp_mail()</code>, so it works with WordPress "
"core, WooCommerce and plugins that use the standard WordPress mail "
"function. It supports plain-text and HTML messages, Reply-To, CC, BCC and "
"up to two attachments. If MailBridgeAPI is disconnected, WordPress returns "
"to its original mail transport."
msgstr ""
"El plugin intercepta <code>wp_mail()</code>, por lo que funciona con el "
"núcleo de WordPress, WooCommerce y los plugins que utilizan la función de "
"correo estándar de WordPress. Admite mensajes de texto sin formato y HTML, "
"Reply-To, CC, CCO y hasta dos archivos adjuntos. Si MailBridgeAPI se "
"desconecta, WordPress vuelve a su transporte de correo original."

# polyglots: glossary term not used: "authentication" -> "identificación"
# polyglots: "autentica" -> "identificar / identificación" (Glossary: authenticate/authentication - use "identificar/identificación", never "autenticar/autenticación".)
# polyglots: The glossary requires 'authentication' to be translated as 'identificación'.
#. Found in description paragraph.
msgid ""
"The dashboard password is used only for the HTTPS authentication request "
"and is never stored. The account token and selected API keys are encrypted "
"with AES-256-GCM using a key derived from the WordPress authentication salt."
msgstr ""
"La contraseña del escritorio solo se utiliza para la solicitud de "
"identificación HTTPS y nunca se almacena. El token de la cuenta y las "
"claves API seleccionadas se cifran con AES-256-GCM mediante una clave "
"derivada de la sal de identificación de WordPress."

# polyglots: glossary term not used: "code" -> "código" / "programar"; "dashboard" -> "escritorio"
# polyglots: "autentica" -> "identificar / identificación" (Glossary: authenticate/authentication - use "identificar/identificación", never "autenticar/autenticación".)
# polyglots: The glossary requires 'authenticated' to be translated as 'identificado'.
#. Found in description list item.
msgid ""
"<code>https://dashboard.mailbridgeapi.com/api/mobile/v1/mailboxes/</code> "
"returns mailboxes belonging to the authenticated account."
msgstr ""
"<code>https://dashboard.mailbridgeapi.com/api/mobile/v1/mailboxes/</code> "
"devuelve los buzones que pertenecen a la cuenta identificada."

# polyglots: glossary term not used: "code" -> "código" / "programar"; "email" -> "correo electrónico"; "locale" -> "configuración regional"; "login" -> "acceder / acceso"; "notification" -> "aviso"
# polyglots: "autentica" -> "identificar / identificación" (Glossary: authenticate/authentication - use "identificar/identificación", never "autenticar/autenticación".)
# polyglots: "notific" -> "aviso / avisar" (Glossary: notification/notify - use "aviso/avisar", never "notificación/notificar".)
# polyglots: Glossary: email address - use "dirección de correo electrónico".
# polyglots: The glossary requires 'authenticate' as 'identificar', 'email' as 'correo electrónico', 'locale' as 'configuración regional', 'login' as 'acceder' and 'notification' as 'aviso'.
# polyglots: The glossary requires 'authenticate' as 'identificar', 'email' as 'correo electrónico', 'locale' as 'configuración regional', 'login' as 'acceder' and 'notification' as 'aviso'.
#. Found in description list item.
msgid ""
"<code>https://dashboard.mailbridgeapi.com/api/mobile/v1/auth/login/</code> "
"authenticates the administrator. It receives the dashboard email address "
"and password, this site's host name, plugin version, WordPress locale and "
"notification preference."
msgstr ""
"<code>https://dashboard.mailbridgeapi.com/api/mobile/v1/auth/login/</code> "
"identifica al administrador. Recibe la dirección de correo electrónico y la "
"contraseña del escritorio, el nombre de host de este sitio, la versión del "
"plugin, la configuración regional de WordPress y la preferencia de avisos."

# polyglots: glossary term not used: "email" -> "correo electrónico"
# polyglots: "autentica" -> "identificar / identificación" (Glossary: authenticate/authentication - use "identificar/identificación", never "autenticar/autenticación".)
# polyglots: Glossary: email - use "correo electrónico" ("dirección de correo electrónico"). Ignore product names and code.
# polyglots: Use 'correo electrónico' instead of 'correo' and 'identifica' instead of 'autentica' as per glossary rules.
# polyglots: Use 'correo electrónico' instead of 'correo' and 'identifica' instead of 'autentica' as per glossary rules.
#. Found in description paragraph.
msgid ""
"MailBridgeAPI Email Delivery connects WordPress to a mailbox that is "
"centrally managed in MailBridgeAPI. It does not ask for or store the "
"mailbox SMTP password in WordPress. After an administrator authenticates "
"the MailBridgeAPI account and locks one mailbox to the site, outgoing "
"messages are delivered through the MailBridgeAPI HTTPS API."
msgstr ""
"MailBridgeAPI Email Delivery conecta WordPress a un buzón gestionado de "
"forma centralizada en MailBridgeAPI. No solicita ni almacena en WordPress "
"la contraseña SMTP del buzón. Cuando un administrador identifica la cuenta "
"de MailBridgeAPI y bloquea un buzón para el sitio, los mensajes salientes "
"se entregan mediante la API HTTPS de MailBridgeAPI."

# polyglots: glossary term not used: "email" -> "correo electrónico"
# polyglots: Use 'correo electrónico' instead of 'correo'.
#. Found in description list item.
msgid ""
"Send a real end-to-end test email and inspect its MailBridgeAPI message "
"identifier."
msgstr ""
"Envía un correo electrónico de prueba real de extremo a extremo y consulta "
"su identificador de mensaje de MailBridgeAPI."

# polyglots: "iniciar sesión" -> "acceder" (Glossary: login - use "Acceder", never "Iniciar sesión".)
# polyglots: Use 'acceder' instead of 'iniciar sesión'.
#. Found in description list item.
msgid ""
"After selection, the plugin hides every other account mailbox. Changing the "
"mailbox requires a complete disconnect and a new sign-in."
msgstr ""
"Tras la selección, el plugin oculta todos los demás buzones de la cuenta. "
"Para cambiar de buzón es necesario desconectarse por completo y acceder de "
"nuevo."

# polyglots: glossary term not used: "email" -> "correo electrónico"; "sign in" -> "acceder"
# polyglots: "inicia sesión" -> "accede" (Glossary: login - use "Acceder", never "Iniciar sesión".)
# polyglots: Glossary: email address - use "dirección de correo electrónico".
# polyglots: Use 'accede' instead of 'inicia sesión' and 'dirección de correo electrónico' instead of 'dirección de correo'.
# polyglots: Use 'accede' instead of 'inicia sesión' and 'dirección de correo electrónico' instead of 'dirección de correo'.
#. Found in description list item.
msgid ""
"Sign in using the email address and password used for the MailBridgeAPI "
"dashboard."
msgstr ""
"Accede con la dirección de correo electrónico y la contraseña utilizadas "
"para el escritorio de MailBridgeAPI."

# polyglots: glossary term not used: "email" -> "correo electrónico"
# polyglots: The glossary term 'email' must be translated as 'correo electrónico'.
#. Found in changelog list item.
#, gp-priority: low
msgid "Local sent-email log, filters, statistics and automatic retention cleanup."
msgstr ""
"Registro local de correos electrónicos enviados, filtros, estadísticas y "
"limpieza automática según la conservación configurada."

# polyglots: glossary term not used: "email" -> "correo electrónico"
# polyglots: The glossary term 'email' must be translated as 'correo electrónico'.
#. Found in changelog list item.
#, gp-priority: low
msgid "Secure dashboard email/password connection and locked mailbox selection."
msgstr ""
"Conexión segura con el correo electrónico y la contraseña del Escritorio y "
"selección bloqueada del buzón."

# polyglots: glossary term not used: "code" -> "código" / "programar"; "email" -> "correo electrónico"
# polyglots: The source 'Add' should be translated as 'Añadir' or an imperative; 'Añadido' is a past participle and doesn't fit the command context. Also, 'email' must be 'correo electrónico'.
#. Found in changelog list item.
#, gp-priority: low
msgid ""
"Add the <code>mailbridgeapi_email_delivery_source</code> filter for "
"specialised WordPress integrations."
msgstr ""
"Añadir el filtro <code>mailbridgeapi_email_delivery_source</code> para "
"integraciones especializadas de WordPress."

# polyglots: The source 'Add' is a command and should be translated as 'Añadir' or an imperative, not the past participle 'Añadida'.
#. Found in changelog list item.
#, gp-priority: low
msgid "Add the translation template."
msgstr "Añadir la plantilla de traducción."

# polyglots: glossary term not used: "email" -> "correo electrónico"
# polyglots: The glossary term for 'email' is 'correo electrónico'.
#. Found in changelog list item.
#, gp-priority: low
msgid "Detect common competing SMTP and email delivery plugins."
msgstr ""
"Se añade la detección de plugins SMTP y de entrega de correo electrónico "
"habituales que pueden entrar en conflicto."

# polyglots: glossary term not used: "email" -> "correo electrónico"
# polyglots: The glossary term for 'email' is 'correo electrónico'.
# polyglots: the model's fix was kept, but brought in what the submitted text did not have: glossary ("add" -> "añadir")
#. Found in changelog list item.
#, gp-priority: low
msgid ""
"Add real end-to-end test email delivery with persistent provider result and "
"message ID."
msgstr ""
"Se añade la entrega real de correos de prueba de extremo a extremo con "
"resultado persistente del proveedor e ID de mensaje."
